slates anchor: a start's busiest thread is judged spinning past 1000 ms of CPU without a beat at least (the liveness window held to this build, A-318; the window is longer where this anchor's own waits run later, A-461)
slates anchor: a crash loop backs off from its failed start's own life, doubling to 6000 ms: backoff_cap_ns = nfs_v4_lease_ns: a crash loop's doubling stops at the NFSv4 lease the daemon grants, so a client renewing at its floor finds the daemon back before its lease runs out (anchors ["nfs_v4_lease_ns"])
