slates anchor: a daemon's beat is lapsed once older than the 1000 ms liveness window plus this anchor's own measured lateness p99, over its last 100 timed waits, at most 10000 ms (the daemon's observation budget); a running daemon is looked at again within that bound less the lateness p99 and a 100 ms beat, at least a beat apart (A-467)
slates anchor: a starting daemon is judged until its watchdog takes the beat over, each of its beats a step: killed once it has neither beaten nor made CPU progress for its window, or one of its threads has run that window of CPU held to this build without a beat, in its own CPU time (read from the OS, each thread's); its window is the 1000 ms liveness window, raised to how late this anchor's own waits run where that is longer (A-461)
